# Platform Dashboard - Cursor Rules

## Architecture Principles

- Use Server Components by default
- Only add "use client" for interactive components
- Follow TypeScript strict mode (no 'any' types)
- Use Zod for all validation schemas
- Use TanStack Table for all data tables
- Use TanStack Query for API caching
- Use React Hook Form for complex forms

## Code Style

- Follow the patterns in design.md
- Use composition over prop drilling
- Keep components focused (single responsibility)
- Name files in kebab-case (user-table.tsx)
- Use named exports for components

## API Integration

- Backend location: ../laratenant-backend/
- Always read backend controllers for API contracts
- Use centralized API client (lib/api/client.ts)
- Handle errors with user-friendly messages
- Map Laravel ErrorCode enum to frontend messages

## Internationalization

- All UI text must use translation keys
- Support English (en) and Arabic (ar)
- Use RTL-aware Tailwind classes (rtl:ml-4)
- Test both LTR and RTL layouts

## Security

- Never trust client-provided auth data
- Always validate on server (Server Actions)
- Use httpOnly cookies for auth tokens
- Implement CSRF protection
- Server-side authorization on all mutations

## Testing

- Write unit tests for utilities and business logic
- Write component tests for forms and tables
- Write E2E tests for critical workflows
- Run accessibility tests (jest-axe)
- Test incrementally at each checkpoint

## Quality

- No console.log in production code
- Fix TypeScript errors immediately
- Fix ESLint warnings
- Maintain consistent code style (Prettier)
- Add loading states for async operations
- Add error boundaries for error handling
